	)
	(text "1) PREVENT SELF-OSCILLATIONS:\nsince in the event of a short circuit \nthere is a strong tendency to self-oscillate \nit may be necessary to review (downwards) \nC18 and/or C22 values\n\n2) SCALE TRANSFORMER VOLTAGE:\nincrease R1 and R2. Example:\n36V ac : R1=150ohm 3W, R42=82ohm 3W \n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.092 47.752 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(color 255 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "bdf5389f-005d-48b5-8be5-360dc224ba87")
	)
	(text "Current\noffset"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 139.7 123.19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ec262bd0-32ae-4024-a15f-282854c3382f")
	)
	(text "3) SCALE CURRENT:\nadd 1 power transistor and 2 resistors every 2A.\nFurthermore, the values of R12 and R23 must be proportionally decreased \nas well as appropriately modifying the firmware. L1 will also have to\nwithstand the desired current. Examples: \n5 final transistor (10A) R23=15k and R24=1500\n2 final transistor (3A) R23=22k and R24=2700"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 155.448 42.926 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(color 255 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ecc97b2e-a36a-4e7b-ab43-dd413b58cafb")
	)
